WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.567
-Hi, buddy. How are you?

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.036
-I'm good. How's it going?

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.503
-I'm doing really well.

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:06.639
Hey, congratulations
on this movie.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.109
As you know, I love it.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.110
-Well, thank you very much.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.611
-[ Laughs ]
Oh, look at that.

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:15.381
You have the mug.
-Oh!

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:16.415
This is your show!

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:17.917
I use it so much, I forgot

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.885
it even has anything
to do with you.

00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:23.923
-Oh, that's so kind of you,
Andy.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:28.561
I wish I had -- you know,
they actually did send some swag

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.630
from your movie "Palm Springs."

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.832
I'm going to prove
this is not planned

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:36.536
because otherwise I would
have had it, but...

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.806
-I can just talk to the sea
captain while you're gone.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.307
Hey, man.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.810
-Look, this is a for-real thing
that showed up.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.545
-Oh, nice! Yeah. From the movie.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.446
-Yeah.
It's a blow-up piece of pizza.

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:48.781
And it actually says

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:52.284
"as seen in the Hulu original
film 'Palm Springs.'"

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.854
-It's easy to do promos
like that when your props

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.323
cost very, very little money.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:01:00.660
-So you obviously did not
film this movie

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.863
thinking it would only
be available on Hulu

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.898
because it was made
in a different time.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:11.004
-Correct, pre-COVID.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.739
-It actually is
a pretty good movie

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:15.641
for the times we're living in,
though.

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.476
I mean, it's super funny,

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.845
but it's also, like,
really thoughtful

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:23.182
and lovely performances
from you and Cristin.

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:26.485
But it's a good -- it's a "good
times we're living in" movie.

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:30.490
-It definitely makes you think
about what it's like

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.093
when you're forced to sit with
yourself and face who you are.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.761
And, you know,
there's a cyclical nature

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:37.696
to the lives we are
living right now.

00:01:37.696 --> 00:01:42.802
-Yes. This is another -- a film
about a guy who might not know

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.236
exactly how much time
has passed,

00:01:44.236 --> 00:01:46.205
which I think we all
are right now.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.873
-Yes. I also just want to
quickly say

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:50.042
I got the memo
that we should dress identical.

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:51.844
And thank you for sending that.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.146
-Of course.
You're very welcome.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.247
-I want to confuse people
as much as possible

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:57.083
watching as to who is who.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.984
-Yeah.
I think that's really good.

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:01.787
I think ultimately we probably
won't do this with sound.

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.356
So it'll just --
it'll just be --

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:06.358
-Oh, great.

00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:09.829
-Hey, you know, again,
I really love the film.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:14.166
I took to Instagram to say it,
and I apologize that my dog --

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.135
obviously, anyone who knows you

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.137
and I know that you're not a fan
of my dog Frisbee.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.105
-Right.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:22.942
-And basically my Instagram post

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.912
was that Frisbee had no interest
in seeing "Palm Springs"

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:29.448
and said she would prefer to put
her nose close to her butthole.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:33.886
-Right. I mean, I saw the post,
and I want to say, first off,

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:35.889
thank you for the kind words
about the movie.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.323
-Yeah.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.558
-And, second, it was actually
an interesting thing

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:42.962
because when I saw the post,
the picture of Frisbee --

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.363
there was a moment
when I first saw it

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.566
where I was, like, "Oh, yes!"

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.300
Because in the picture,

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.637
it almost looks like Frisbee
is dead, you know?

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.672
-Uh-huh.
-Has passed on.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.573
-Yeah.
-And is no longer with us.

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:56.242
-Uh-huh.
-Which, to me was, like,

00:02:56.242 --> 00:03:00.413
"Whoa, Seth liked the movie,
and the rat is dead."

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.381
-Oh, so, like, for you
it was a win-win?

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:04.083
-It was jubilation.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.518
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:09.022
But then I read the caption
and I realized

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.890
it was kind of a burn,
and I was like...

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.224
-Right.

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:17.363
-"That's funny, but I wish
Frisbee was dead."

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.899
-You really take advantage of
this opportunity

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.600
like when you're on the show.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.903
You are in the safety of
a television studio.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.972
And you've laid into Frisbee
pretty hard over the years.

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.341
-That's true.
-Yeah.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:31.044
So I guess if you would just
bear with me for a second.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.846
-Sure.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.981
Sea Captain.

00:03:35.981 --> 00:03:38.951
-You know, 'cause we're doing it
from home now, Samberg.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:40.653
-Sea Captain, are you --

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.289
-And, like, would you say it
to her face?

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.393
-Look.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:50.028
-Look how much she hates you.
Look how much.

00:03:50.028 --> 00:03:51.864
She hates you so much.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:56.101
-Frisbee, I just want to say
it's all in good fun.

00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:58.304
You're a good dog.
-Okay.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:03.643
-Like, it's --
You can't listen to Seth.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:06.612
Don't look at the screen,
Frisbee.

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:08.781
-How did you have that ready?

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.316
-I was going to do it
no matter what!

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.684
Frisbee sucks, dude!

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:12.918
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:14.753
-Alright, Frisbee, I'm going to
let you go, girl.

00:04:14.753 --> 00:04:18.257
Don't come back until you have
tonight's pheasants for dinner.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:20.059
-I'm actually kind of
lightheaded now.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.894
I hate confrontation.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.429
You did really well.
-Thank you.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.898
-I thought you did really well.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:29.869
You are a very -- I've said --
yeah, thank you.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.838
You were a great actor always.

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:34.674
You're particularly good
in this film.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.842
-Thank you.
-And it should be noted

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:39.078
that Cristin Milioti
is a wonderful co-star.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.245
The two of you were great.

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:41.781
-She's actually good.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:44.550
-Did you ever feel like at "SNL"

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.520
you had a scene where you
thought, "Oh, I'm a good actor"?

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:52.291
-You know, I never felt it
deep down personally,

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.193
but I will say this.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:58.030
There was a sketch
when Galifianakis hosted

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:00.466
where I was the straight man
in it.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:03.469
And afterwards a lot of people
at the show --

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.805
like, writers
and casts and people

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:06.873
who worked at the show
were like,

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.307
"Hey, man, you were really good
in that.

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:09.308
You really grounded it."

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:11.877
And the sketch was called
"Bidet."

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:13.145
-[ Laughs ]
I remember "Bidet."

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:16.649
-It was a sketch where Zach
and Wiig are at a --

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.384
I'm showing them around a hotel.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.886
I'm, like, the fancy bell boy,

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:22.788
and they just keep asking
questions about the bidet.

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.723
They're like,
"And what about the bidet?

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:26.526
Does it have a sturdiness
to it?"

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:28.460
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:31.263
And I guess good acting
in this context

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:33.399
was just not laughing
because I really did want to.

